{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99337","id":2183385131,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6CI9Ar","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99337","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99337.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99337.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99337","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99337/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99337/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99337/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/80ade273c474896b621af7054c70ba7c361f9c9a","number":99337,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Use correct coefficients to get luminance from a color in linear space","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114) should be used with gamma corrected SRGB colors, not with linear colors.\r\n\r\nfixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/57015\r\n\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/a/56678483\r\n\r\n```\r\nTO FIND LUMINANCE:\r\n\r\n...Because apparently it was lost somewhere...\r\n\r\nStep One:\r\n\r\nConvert all sRGB 8 bit integer values to decimal 0.0-1.0\r\n\r\n  vR = sR / 255;\r\n  vG = sG / 255;\r\n  vB = sB / 255;\r\nStep Two:\r\n\r\nConvert a gamma encoded RGB to a linear value. sRGB (computer standard) for instance requires a power curve of approximately V^2.2, though the \"accurate\" transform is:\r\n\r\nsRGB to Linear\r\n\r\nWhere V´ is the gamma-encoded R, G, or B channel of sRGB.\r\nPseudocode:\r\n\r\nfunction sRGBtoLin(colorChannel) {\r\n        // Send this function a decimal sRGB gamma encoded color value\r\n        // between 0.0 and 1.0, and it returns a linearized value.\r\n\r\n    if ( colorChannel <= 0.04045 ) {\r\n            return colorChannel / 12.92;\r\n        } else {\r\n            return pow((( colorChannel + 0.055)/1.055),2.4);\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\nStep Three:\r\n\r\nTo find Luminance (Y) apply the standard coefficients for sRGB:\r\n\r\nApply coefficients Y = R * 0.2126 + G * 0.7152 + B *  0.0722 \r\n\r\nPseudocode using above functions:\r\n\r\nY = (0.2126 * sRGBtoLin(vR) + 0.7152 * sRGBtoLin(vG) + 0.0722 * sRGBtoLin(vB))\r\n```","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/go